/-!
# Structurality from `Equation3364` through the companion `x □ y = (x ◇ (x ◇ (x ◇ y)))`

Generated by `defwork/wffit.py`.  `Equation3364` is `x ◇ y = y ◇ (z ◇ (x ◇ z))`.  The source half is
`AutBox.WordRigidFull`: two finite models of `Equation3364` on one carrier with the same table of
`(x ◇ (x ◇ (x ◇ y)))` are the same model.  That is what makes the companion's automorphisms automorphisms of
`◇`, and it mentions no map, so `grind` can do it.  Each theorem below then only has to check that
the source forces its target of the companion.
-/

open FirstOrder FirstOrder.Language Law Law.MagmaLaw FreeMagma

set_option maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false
